.TH "FLOX\-SERVICES\-RESTART" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-services\-restart \- restart running services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general\-options>] services restart
     [\-d=<path> | \-r=<owner/name>]
     [<name>] ...
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Restarts the specified services.
.PP
If no services are specified, stops all running services and starts new
services using the latest build of the environment.
If one or more services are running, then the specified services are
started using the service config that the running services were started
with.
.PP
When all services are restarted, they are started from an ephemeral
activation that uses the latest build of the environment.
This may not be the build of the environment that your shell has
activated, so the environment variables present for services may be
different from the ones in your shell.
To ensure that your shell and the services have the same environment,
reactivate your environment after making edits to the manifest.
.PP
An error is displayed if the specified service does not exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]<name>\f[R]
The name(s) of the services to restart.
.SS Environment Options
If no environment is specified for an environment command, the
environment in the current directory or the active environment that was
last activated is used.
.TP
\f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R]
Path containing a .flox/ directory.
.TP
\f[CR]\-r\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R]
A FloxHub environment, specified in the form \f[CR]<owner>/<name>\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-D\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-default\f[R]
Use your default environment (\f[CR]<your\-user>/default\f[R]).
When unauthenticated in an interactive context, you will be prompted to
log in.
In non\-interactive contexts (e.g., scripts or CI), this flag will fail
with an error when authentication is missing.
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
Restart a single service:
.IP
.EX
$ flox services restart myservice
✔ Service \(aqmyservice\(aq restarted.
.EE
.PP
Restart all services:
.IP
.EX
$ flox services restart
✔ Service \(aqservice1\(aq restarted.
✔ Service \(aqservice2\(aq restarted.
✔ Service \(aqservice3\(aq restarted.
.EE
